# Public canonical origin used for SEO metadata and sitemap generation.
# This is read at build time; rebuild after changing it.
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://sentientwebsite.com/
#
# Optional: Sentient/Robanka live assistant widget.
# Omit both values to run the marketing site without the agent.
# VITE_ is preferred in Vite; NEXT_PUBLIC_ names are also supported (see vite.config envPrefix).
#
# Compliance gate before enabling in production:
# - Public legal routes must be live: /privacy, /terms, /cookies, /ai-disclosure, /data-request.
# - The ConsentManager must remain mounted so the widget loads only after visitor consent.
# - The 18+ confirmation must remain enabled before assistant loading.
# - Robanka DPA, Google/Gemini terms, retention, deletion, region, and model-training controls must be approved.
# - Run: npm run lint && npm test && npm run build && npm run test:e2e:no-build
#
# In Docker/Render, the server also exposes these values through /sentient-widget-config.json.
# The client prefers that runtime config over bundled build-time Vite config.
# The install key is a public client identifier, not a server secret. Scope it by allowed
# origins in Robanka/SentientWeb admin, rotate it when needed, and do not use it for
# server-side authorization.
# Production widget origins must use https. Plain http is accepted only for local hosts
# such as localhost or 127.0.0.1 during development.
#
# VITE_SENTIENT_WIDGET_ORIGIN=https://cdn.example.com
# VITE_SENTIENT_INSTALL_KEY=your-install-key
#
# Optional: force HSTS on/off for production-like hosts that do not set NODE_ENV=production.
# SENTIENT_HSTS_ENABLED=true
#
# Optional: reject requests whose Host header is not in this comma-separated allow-list.
# Leave unset for local development, preview URLs, or platforms that manage host routing upstream.
# Use *.onrender.com for Render Blueprint previews when this guard is enabled there.
# SENTIENT_ALLOWED_HOSTS=sentientwebsite.com,www.sentientwebsite.com,*.onrender.com
#
# Server-side consent evidence logging is required for production operations.
# Store JSONL evidence outside dist/ and outside public web roots; production evidence custody is
# restricted Google Workspace/Drive or an equivalent access-controlled operations location.
# Configure a high-entropy salt so request IP/user-agent values are hashed before storage.
# Render deployments mount a persistent disk at /var/data and write consent evidence there.
# Existing Render Blueprint services need SENTIENT_CONSENT_LOG_SALT set manually in the dashboard.
# SENTIENT_CONSENT_LOG_PATH=/var/data/sentientweb/consent-events.jsonl
# SENTIENT_CONSENT_LOG_SALT=replace-with-high-entropy-secret
